ie Hobbs (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Arizona's governor race pits incumbent Democrat Katie Hobbs against Republican congressman Andy Biggs. Polling throughout October has been remarkably consistent: even Republican-leaning pollsters show Hobbs ahead, with recent surveys giving her leads of 6 to 13 points among likely voters. Fundraising heavily favors Hobbs, who has raised roughly three times as much as Biggs, and prediction markets price her chances around 90% or better.\n\nExpert raters mostly call the race Likely or Lean Democratic, with the most bullish putting it at Solid D. Biggs' hard-right profile and the contest's framing around election certification have complicated Republican closing arguments, and reporting suggests GOP allies see the race slipping. The state's Republican lean of about two points is outweighed by incumbency and a favorable environment for Hobbs. A late shift in turnout dynamics remains the main source of uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 7.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9047, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9201, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9198, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8839, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8882, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8963, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8934, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8924, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8871, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8786, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8851, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8914, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8731, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8768, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.879, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8914, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8721, "margin": 6.3}, {"date": "20